  "summary": "Henrico County public works crews removed more than 120 Flock Safety ALPR cameras on Oct. 31 after Flock missed the county's Oct. 21 deadline to take them down following contract termination. The county had notified Flock on Oct. 7 that the contract would end Oct. 14 amid privacy and data-access concerns, and the cameras had already been deactivated before physical removal.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Henrico County crews have removed more than 120 Flock Safety license plate reader cameras after the company missed a deadline to take down the equipment following the termination of its contract with the county.",
